//
// Phase E3: host-only checks on the query-blocked attention that offload and
// runlist share (pattern/blocked_attention.py).
//
// The module is the mode-side implementation of the one boundary the offload
// and runlist strategies keep on the host, written to be arithmetically
// independent of the numpy oracle the golden model uses. These checks pin the
// two implementations against each other on identical bf16 inputs -- the
// comparison no hardware gate performs, because the hardware gate's attention
// inputs already carry device GEMM error -- plus the blocking invariance, the
// scratch-cap thresholds at the two documented ladder rungs, and the scale
// convention against a direct math.exp computation.
//
// No NPU, no XRT and no MLIR: numpy and torch on the host, so this sits beside
// the reference tests and requires neither `ryzen_ai_npu2` nor `peano`.
//
// The test file carries no framework dependency -- pytest is not installed in
// the sandbox venv -- so it runs as a plain script and prints a pass count,
// matched exactly so a test that stops being collected fails here instead of
// passing quietly.
//
// Editing this header: lit scans the WHOLE file for its directives, so naming
// one in prose -- even inside a comment -- registers as a second directive and
// leaves the test UNRESOLVED. Describe them, never spell them out.
//
// RUN: python3 %S/pattern/test_blocked_attention.py | FileCheck %s
//
// CHECK: PASS  test_agrees_with_the_independent_oracle
// CHECK: PASS  test_blocking_does_not_change_the_arithmetic
// CHECK: PASS  test_causal_first_row_attends_only_to_itself
// CHECK: PASS  test_query_block_size_thresholds
// CHECK: PASS  test_scale_is_rsqrt_head_dim
// CHECK: blocked attention tests: 5/5 passed
